WEBVTT

00:41.917 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:53.011 --> 00:54.012
MATH
PART ONE

00:56.139 --> 00:58.392
Just when you start
to get the hang of things,

00:59.476 --> 01:03.939
the chapter you know ends
and an unfamiliar one begins.

01:06.024 --> 01:08.944
Some people rush ahead
to read the final page,

01:09.444 --> 01:12.364
but I was the type
to run away from the ending.

01:13.657 --> 01:16.076
The type who can't let go
of the main character

01:16.159 --> 01:18.120
and leaves the final volume unread,

01:18.203 --> 01:22.833
and the type who never beats
the final boss so the game won't end.

01:26.044 --> 01:29.131
Maybe it's because
I already knew that deep down,

01:30.257 --> 01:32.467
no matter how tightly I held on,

01:32.551 --> 01:35.804
I couldn't stop the ending from coming.

01:35.902 --> 01:41.810
FINAL EPISODE
THE END IS A NEW BEGINNING

01:44.771 --> 01:47.733
I guess the smart ones
handle despair differently.

01:48.567 --> 01:52.446
If it were me, I'd just fall apart.
I'd spend my days crying and sleeping.

01:52.988 --> 01:56.241
Even in the midst of such despair,
you kept looking for solutions.

01:56.742 --> 01:59.494
I'm no different. I'm just flailing here.

02:00.245 --> 02:01.955
I know there's no way out of this.

02:04.416 --> 02:05.709
What did the doctor say?

02:05.792 --> 02:08.337
Luckily, it hasn't gotten any worse,

02:09.171 --> 02:11.131
but I don't think it'll get better.

02:11.214 --> 02:14.301
Still, I want to try everything I can.

02:14.384 --> 02:15.969
Meds, treatments, anything.

02:16.470 --> 02:18.055
Take the meds now.

02:20.307 --> 02:23.185
Gosh, there are so many pills…

02:25.646 --> 02:27.939
- I already took them.
- What?

02:28.023 --> 02:32.027
You weren't talking about your meds
when you said you left something at home?

02:32.110 --> 02:33.445
Before we get to that…

02:34.738 --> 02:36.114
there's something I want to say.

02:38.533 --> 02:40.285
What now?

02:40.994 --> 02:42.329
I want to apologize properly.

02:43.288 --> 02:45.582
I didn't want you to get hurt,

02:45.666 --> 02:47.542
but I ended up hurting you even more.

02:48.585 --> 02:51.171
I thought being on my own
would make me less of a burden,

02:52.839 --> 02:54.591
but I didn't realize how selfish that was.

02:54.675 --> 02:55.550
I'm sorry.

03:00.389 --> 03:01.515
How can you…

03:02.224 --> 03:03.308
be like this?

03:04.726 --> 03:07.396
It took me ten years to figure that out,

03:07.479 --> 03:09.272
and I still had no idea what to do.

03:09.356 --> 03:11.608
So I just wanted to be with you.

03:11.692 --> 03:12.776
If you had said no,

03:12.859 --> 03:15.404
I was ready to camp out
in front of your place.

03:16.238 --> 03:18.907
I never thought you'd come to me first.

03:19.408 --> 03:20.826
You're not like me.

03:21.702 --> 03:22.953
You really are…

03:24.413 --> 03:26.164
a better person than I am.

03:28.208 --> 03:31.294
Honestly, nothing has changed.

03:31.837 --> 03:34.798
My ears are the same,
and I don't know what will happen next.

03:34.881 --> 03:37.217
And surely, being by my side will be hard.

03:39.094 --> 03:40.178
Even so…

03:42.139 --> 03:43.432
I want to be with you.

03:45.434 --> 03:46.601
Even if it's hard,

03:47.894 --> 03:49.813
I want to stick it out together.

03:51.356 --> 03:52.816
Hey.

03:52.899 --> 03:55.527
Why do you keep saying
what I should be saying?

03:55.610 --> 03:57.195
Now I've got nothing to say.

03:58.488 --> 03:59.489
Jeez.

04:02.784 --> 04:03.869
Hey…

04:06.246 --> 04:07.289
Here.

04:17.299 --> 04:19.426
Ho-su, when did you…

04:22.554 --> 04:23.638
Put it on.

04:28.059 --> 04:29.519
How does it fit so perfectly?

04:33.815 --> 04:36.568
Hey, when did you put that ring on?

04:39.112 --> 04:40.322
Do you like it?

04:43.241 --> 04:44.951
Ho-su.

04:46.119 --> 04:47.329
Thank you.

04:47.412 --> 04:49.790
This is so pretty.

04:53.710 --> 04:55.378
By the way,

04:55.462 --> 04:58.465
can you actually catch any fish here?

04:58.548 --> 05:00.509
We're fishing for time.

05:00.592 --> 05:01.676
FARM OPERATION PLAN

05:01.760 --> 05:04.346
Do we really need these contracts
and business license stuff?

05:04.429 --> 05:07.140
It seems like a hassle.
It'd be easier to just run it as is.

05:08.016 --> 05:09.893
I think it's better to get things sorted

05:09.976 --> 05:12.646
so we can apply for young farmer
support funds or subsidies later on.

05:12.729 --> 05:15.232
You already have a lot to worry about,

05:15.315 --> 05:18.735
and it wouldn't feel right to keep asking
someone in the States for help.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.280
I like that idea. I'm okay with it.

05:22.364 --> 05:23.782
I'm not, though.

05:25.158 --> 05:27.869
I just want to try running a business
under my own name.

05:28.829 --> 05:32.374
I thought you were all by the book.
Turns out you're quite ambitious.

05:32.457 --> 05:35.710
But do you have money?
Running a business requires money.

05:35.794 --> 05:37.671
I have my severance pay,

05:37.754 --> 05:41.174
so I'll use that
to build a stock portfolio.

05:41.967 --> 05:44.511
And I'm thinking of starting a blog too.

05:44.594 --> 05:46.847
A blog? About farming?

05:46.930 --> 05:49.140
No, an investment blog.

05:49.224 --> 05:52.185
Like the one you used to run,
"Se-jinvestor."

05:53.645 --> 05:55.689
How do you know Se-jinvestor?

05:57.148 --> 06:00.068
You somehow know everything about me.

06:00.652 --> 06:03.196
I got a lot of tips from that blog.

06:03.280 --> 06:07.701
So I figured I'd go ahead and share
my investment ideas like that too.

06:08.743 --> 06:12.372
Maybe you could take a look sometime.

06:13.331 --> 06:15.458
I charge for consulting, you know.

06:17.252 --> 06:19.212
Okay, it's free for a business partner.

06:20.130 --> 06:22.549
By the way, about that house.

06:22.632 --> 06:24.885
Would it be okay if I lived there?

06:24.968 --> 06:26.595
Sure, I don't mind.

06:27.429 --> 06:30.307
But wouldn't staying at your mom's
be better for you?

06:30.390 --> 06:33.977
It'd save time on commuting,
and I'm more comfortable living alone.

06:35.270 --> 06:39.691
Is it okay if I make some changes
while I'm living there?

06:40.400 --> 06:42.903
You got super upset that time
I threw out the chair.

06:42.986 --> 06:44.613
That was ages ago.

06:45.906 --> 06:47.574
Sorry about that again.

06:50.076 --> 06:52.370
Even if you tear the place down
and pitch a tent,

06:52.454 --> 06:54.331
I won't say a word. Promise.

06:55.165 --> 06:56.333
Jeez.

06:56.958 --> 06:58.126
Thank you.

07:01.338 --> 07:03.256
How about this?

07:03.340 --> 07:06.343
I invest the initial capital
and take eight.

07:06.426 --> 07:08.970
That's not very fair.

07:09.888 --> 07:11.139
Ninety-two to eight.

07:12.098 --> 07:14.184
That's not fair either.

07:14.267 --> 07:16.311
We don't even know
how profitable it will be.

07:16.394 --> 07:19.064
That's how investing works.

07:19.147 --> 07:21.107
If you don't like it, stick to savings.

07:21.191 --> 07:22.817
It's like fishing.

07:22.901 --> 07:24.945
If you catch something, great.

07:25.028 --> 07:27.489
If you don't,
at least you got some meditation in.

07:28.156 --> 07:30.784
- Look, it moved.
- What? Why?

07:30.867 --> 07:31.826
- How?
- Just now.

07:31.910 --> 07:34.454
I'm scared of fish. You do it, quick!

07:34.537 --> 07:36.790
- Why are you fishing, then?
- Get the scoop net!

07:36.873 --> 07:39.292
- Shouldn't we pull it up first?
- Then pull it up.

07:39.376 --> 07:40.543
- What do I…
- No!

07:43.004 --> 07:45.090
Didn't we decide
to do this part like this?

07:45.173 --> 07:47.050
- Yes.
- But look over there!

07:47.133 --> 07:48.969
The left side is way too low!

07:49.594 --> 07:52.305
- She might go up there herself soon.
- Lower the right side.

07:52.389 --> 07:53.598
She really might.

07:53.682 --> 07:55.809
Yes. Now that's too low.

07:55.892 --> 07:58.311
You never laughed
when she wasn't around, did you?

07:58.395 --> 07:59.854
Right there. Try leveling it…

07:59.938 --> 08:02.607
I'm sorry for making you worry about me.

08:02.691 --> 08:05.151
We're way past apologizing
for things like that.

08:05.235 --> 08:06.528
Gently to the right.

08:06.611 --> 08:08.655
No matter how hard your day is,

08:08.738 --> 08:11.950
one second of laughter
can get you through it.

08:12.993 --> 08:14.411
Be careful.

08:14.494 --> 08:18.415
So don't ever let go of the person
who makes you laugh.

08:20.500 --> 08:23.753
Come on. We're putting up the sign.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.007
Hurry up.

08:29.009 --> 08:30.260
- Thank you.
- Sure.

08:30.343 --> 08:32.345
- Call if you need anything.
- Okay. Take care!

08:32.429 --> 08:34.597
ROSA RESTAURANT
SERVING CHICKEN GIBLET STEW FOR 35 YEARS

08:34.681 --> 08:37.350
Ho-su, shouldn't you be heading
to the hospital for your appointment?

08:37.434 --> 08:39.102
I'll be fine if I leave now.

08:39.185 --> 08:41.271
Ms. Sang-wol, I'll get going.

08:41.354 --> 08:42.605
Okay.

08:43.648 --> 08:44.816
I'll call you.

08:46.860 --> 08:49.988
If you have time, how about some coffee?

08:50.739 --> 08:52.198
What's this?

08:52.282 --> 08:54.034
Such a classic pickup line.

08:55.243 --> 08:56.411
Let's go.

08:59.247 --> 09:01.708
Let me open the door for you.

09:12.552 --> 09:14.220
- Thank you.
- Sure.

09:25.648 --> 09:29.402
I never thought I'd see the day
when this place would feel peaceful.

09:30.445 --> 09:31.654
Now that the sign's up,

09:31.738 --> 09:35.867
doesn't it feel like
more sunlight is coming in?

09:37.285 --> 09:41.372
We only changed the sign.
Everything else is the same.

09:41.456 --> 09:43.374
The shop's name hasn't changed,

09:43.458 --> 09:46.878
and I'm still selling chicken giblet stew.

09:49.798 --> 09:53.927
But now that my name's changed,
it feels different.

09:56.262 --> 09:58.098
It's like all these locked doors

09:59.099 --> 10:00.683
unlocked at the same time,

10:01.351 --> 10:03.895
and now I don't know
which one to open first.

10:07.524 --> 10:10.026
I heard you decided
to start treatment for dyslexia.

10:10.652 --> 10:15.198
I kept saying there was no point
in learning anything,

10:15.281 --> 10:17.450
but Ho-su said
it's something to improve on,

10:17.534 --> 10:21.579
not something to learn,
and insisted that I give it a shot.

10:21.663 --> 10:25.542
He went out of his way
to look into it for me.

10:26.668 --> 10:29.337
I should at least give it a try,
even if it's pointless.

10:31.506 --> 10:32.423
You're amazing.

10:34.259 --> 10:35.260
What?

10:35.802 --> 10:36.678
Are you teasing?

10:36.761 --> 10:39.347
No. I mean it.

10:40.473 --> 10:43.226
When I think I can't do
something very well,

10:43.309 --> 10:46.187
I just make excuses
and pretend not to care.

10:46.729 --> 10:50.400
But you aren't running away
from it like I would.

10:51.109 --> 10:53.027
You're going to try
even if it's pointless.

10:53.111 --> 10:54.445
That's impressive.

10:54.988 --> 10:55.947
Gosh.

10:56.447 --> 11:00.702
If you think I'm amazing,
you should try something pointless too.

11:01.536 --> 11:03.788
That's what I've been thinking about.

11:04.664 --> 11:08.293
Which pointless thing should I try?

11:08.376 --> 11:10.295
I still have to make a living, though.

11:11.129 --> 11:12.172
Gosh.

11:12.714 --> 11:16.092
Speaking of making a living,

11:17.010 --> 11:20.221
have you ever thought
about working with me?

11:21.431 --> 11:22.390
What?

11:22.891 --> 11:26.394
You can learn from me,

11:26.477 --> 11:28.897
and when I'm too old,

11:28.980 --> 11:31.983
you can take over this place.

11:32.066 --> 11:33.443
Then…

11:33.526 --> 11:35.695
you'd at least make a living.

11:37.405 --> 11:40.033
I'm so grateful.

11:40.617 --> 11:44.037
But you're not interested in my offer?

11:44.120 --> 11:45.371
It's not that.

11:45.455 --> 11:49.626
It's such a generous offer,
and I'll definitely think about it.

11:51.044 --> 11:53.421
So you already have
something else in mind?

11:54.380 --> 11:57.508
I kind of do.

11:57.592 --> 12:02.513
But I might end up begging you
to let me work here later.

12:03.181 --> 12:05.099
You'll still accept me then, right?

12:05.183 --> 12:07.018
Just let me know
if you're ever interested,

12:07.101 --> 12:08.978
even if it's just part-time.

12:10.688 --> 12:14.525
Aren't you going to tell me
what you've been thinking about?

12:16.069 --> 12:18.238
It's too early to say.

12:19.280 --> 12:20.865
What is it that's got you all shy?

12:20.949 --> 12:22.825
I'll tell you later.

12:22.909 --> 12:23.868
Gosh.

12:25.828 --> 12:28.790
So what you're saying
is that you're taking over the farm

12:28.873 --> 12:31.000
instead of going back to Seoul?

12:31.501 --> 12:32.502
Yes.

12:35.797 --> 12:36.965
God. It's too fishy.

12:37.507 --> 12:40.677
You've only worked in an office.
How can you handle farming?

12:41.552 --> 12:44.389
I've been doing it all along.

12:45.682 --> 12:47.600
And why live alone out there

12:47.684 --> 12:50.311
when you have
a perfectly good house to live in?

12:50.395 --> 12:52.522
I've been living alone all this time.

12:52.605 --> 12:54.107
But that was in Seoul.

12:54.190 --> 12:57.068
You're the one who said
Seoul was more dangerous.

12:57.819 --> 13:00.530
I'll come visit often.

13:00.613 --> 13:01.698
No, I mean…

13:01.781 --> 13:04.909
After all the work you've done,

13:04.993 --> 13:07.537
now you're talking about farming?
That's more than a waste.

13:07.620 --> 13:08.955
You're wasting your talent.

13:09.038 --> 13:11.499
I'm not saying I'll do it forever.

13:12.125 --> 13:13.459
While running the farm,

13:13.543 --> 13:16.379
I'll keep working on
what I really want to do.

13:16.879 --> 13:20.675
I just want to see if I can do it alone
through my own will and effort,

13:20.758 --> 13:22.343
instead of doing what I'm told.

13:23.303 --> 13:24.595
Gosh.

13:24.679 --> 13:27.015
Didn't you say I should do what I want?

13:28.016 --> 13:29.600
Fine. Do it.

13:30.101 --> 13:31.269
I'm not stopping you.

13:31.978 --> 13:33.313
Go ahead.

13:38.359 --> 13:39.402
What?

13:39.485 --> 13:40.862
Are you Mi-ji?

13:42.113 --> 13:43.114
No.

13:43.656 --> 13:46.826
Really? Mom said, "Go ahead"?

13:47.410 --> 13:51.039
I wish I had been there,
just to see her face.

13:51.539 --> 13:55.668
Anyway, if you still haven't decided
what to do next,

13:55.752 --> 13:57.045
do you want to work with me?

13:57.128 --> 13:59.422
You mean farm work?

13:59.505 --> 14:02.050
I think it'll be tough
to manage on my own at first.

14:02.717 --> 14:04.719
And if you don't want to move back here,

14:04.802 --> 14:06.262
how about once or twice a week?

14:07.055 --> 14:08.639
I'll pay you.

14:08.723 --> 14:10.058
I'll think about it.

14:10.683 --> 14:11.726
Why?

14:11.809 --> 14:14.187
Do you have something else in mind?

14:15.063 --> 14:16.272
No…

14:16.356 --> 14:19.275
Hey, if you're there,
let's do a video call.

14:19.359 --> 14:20.985
I want to see Grandma's face.

14:21.778 --> 14:22.862
Grandma!

14:25.156 --> 14:27.116
Why do you look so tired?

14:27.867 --> 14:29.577
Have you lost weight?

14:30.244 --> 14:31.704
I'm on a diet.

14:32.955 --> 14:37.460
Mi-ji, see if you can convince
Grandma to eat.

14:37.543 --> 14:40.213
What's wrong?
Grandma, have you lost your appetite?

14:40.296 --> 14:42.090
Are you not well?

14:43.508 --> 14:46.135
You know what? I'd better get over there.

14:46.219 --> 14:48.054
And fatten you up.

14:48.137 --> 14:49.972
Don't come.

14:50.056 --> 14:52.517
Why? I miss you.

14:52.600 --> 14:53.976
Should I come today?

14:54.060 --> 14:57.522
No. Don't come.

14:57.605 --> 14:59.690
You don't need to. I'll be with her today.

14:59.774 --> 15:02.860
Why not? I can just drop by.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.529
Don't bother. You're busy.

15:04.612 --> 15:07.532
You've got to get ready
for the move. Don't come.

15:07.615 --> 15:09.117
Did you two plan this?

15:09.200 --> 15:11.202
Why do you keep telling me not to come?

15:11.285 --> 15:13.162
- Gosh.
- I'm hanging up.

15:13.246 --> 15:14.580
Hey!

15:15.123 --> 15:17.708
Jeez. What the heck?

15:17.792 --> 15:19.335
Do I stink or something?

15:19.419 --> 15:21.629
Neither of them wants me to come.

15:21.712 --> 15:24.590
They probably think
it's an important time for you.

15:24.674 --> 15:25.716
What is it?

15:25.800 --> 15:26.968
It's just…

15:27.051 --> 15:29.637
I did say I'd stay in Seoul,

15:29.720 --> 15:32.723
but it feels like they're telling me
not to come until I've made it.

15:32.807 --> 15:35.476
Like they're pushing me to start
before I'm ready.

15:35.977 --> 15:39.480
You spent a long time
by your grandma's side.

15:40.481 --> 15:43.317
They probably think you need
some time for yourself now.

15:43.401 --> 15:45.069
Exactly.

15:45.153 --> 15:46.904
Just because I have time for myself

15:46.988 --> 15:49.615
doesn't mean I'll suddenly
become this amazing person.

15:49.699 --> 15:52.368
It's a lot of pressure.

15:52.452 --> 15:55.371
Mi-ji, no one's expecting
anything like that.

15:57.081 --> 15:59.459
When you put it that way,
it does kind of sting.

16:00.209 --> 16:02.086
They'll have reasonable expectations.

16:02.712 --> 16:05.673
But is Grandma really okay?

16:05.756 --> 16:07.550
She seemed really run-down.

16:07.633 --> 16:10.595
Once you're done moving,

16:10.678 --> 16:12.305
let's visit Duson-ri together.

16:13.139 --> 16:14.056
Okay.

16:14.724 --> 16:17.393
You didn't have to bring this.
I know you're busy as it is.

16:17.477 --> 16:19.479
How did you find time to come?

16:19.562 --> 16:23.024
Mi-rae said she'd stay
with Grandma at the hospital today.

16:23.107 --> 16:24.901
- Mi-rae did?
- Yes.

16:24.984 --> 16:28.613
Even with her crazy schedule,
she still has time for her grandma.

16:30.948 --> 16:32.533
She's been here for a few days.

16:33.576 --> 16:34.911
She's not so busy anymore.

16:35.995 --> 16:37.455
What do you mean?

16:37.538 --> 16:39.499
She quit her job.

16:40.791 --> 16:42.668
She didn't say much,

16:43.878 --> 16:45.588
but I guess it was tough for her.

16:46.172 --> 16:47.507
I see.

16:49.383 --> 16:53.721
Mi-rae will find another good job soon.

16:53.804 --> 16:57.308
She wants to farm.
Over at the strawberry farm.

16:58.976 --> 17:00.102
Who does?

17:01.270 --> 17:03.397
Mi-rae, not Mi-ji?

17:03.481 --> 17:06.859
Yeah. The funny thing is,
Mi-ji's staying in Seoul.

17:07.568 --> 17:09.028
Good God.

17:09.695 --> 17:11.572
They say you never stop worrying
about your kids.

17:11.656 --> 17:14.158
They really are twins,
both worrying me at the same time.

17:14.242 --> 17:15.284
Hey.

17:15.368 --> 17:19.121
You're lucky to have a son like Ho-su.

17:20.331 --> 17:24.085
I need to go to Seoul soon
because of Ho-su.

17:24.919 --> 17:25.920
What for?

17:26.003 --> 17:28.422
His hearing has gotten worse.

17:29.298 --> 17:31.133
I want to be there
during his hospital stay.

17:31.217 --> 17:32.426
Hospital?

17:32.927 --> 17:34.512
Is it that bad?

17:34.595 --> 17:37.473
Well, we'll see how his treatment goes.

17:37.557 --> 17:42.103
Still, thinking back to when he was a kid,
I'm grateful things are not worse.

17:42.895 --> 17:46.107
At least now, it's not life-threatening.

17:46.190 --> 17:47.567
That's true.

17:47.650 --> 17:50.778
We worry about things like this
because they're alive and well.

17:52.405 --> 17:54.782
Is the owner of that strawberry farm

17:54.865 --> 17:58.744
the same one Mi-ji had a thing with?

17:58.828 --> 18:01.122
I told you the rumors are not true!

18:01.205 --> 18:05.084
Bun-hong, Mi-ji is still a kid.

18:05.167 --> 18:07.962
She's not interested in dating.

18:09.630 --> 18:13.134
I used an elite lawyer to help me move.

18:13.217 --> 18:14.802
How should I repay you?

18:15.344 --> 18:16.887
Do I get to choose?

18:17.388 --> 18:20.766
You have two options. Cheek or lips.

18:21.434 --> 18:23.185
Can I choose both?

18:29.114 --> 18:29.984
Mi-ji?

18:31.652 --> 18:32.612
Mom.

18:33.404 --> 18:34.905
How did you…

18:39.327 --> 18:41.579
- Is that you, Ho-su?
- Yes.

18:42.121 --> 18:43.205
Hello.

18:44.624 --> 18:49.170
She's moving,
so I came to help her pack.

18:49.253 --> 18:50.796
What's going on between you two?

18:56.427 --> 18:58.763
It just happened. We're a thing now.

18:58.846 --> 18:59.847
Oh dear.

19:00.765 --> 19:02.433
- Let me get that.
- Yes.

19:02.516 --> 19:03.517
No, it's fine.

19:03.601 --> 19:05.519
- Why should you have to do that?
- Jeez.

19:05.603 --> 19:08.147
Okay. Have you had dinner?

19:08.230 --> 19:10.107
Yes, what time do you think it is?

19:11.025 --> 19:12.026
It's late. You should go.

19:12.109 --> 19:13.694
- Mom.
- Okay.

19:14.236 --> 19:15.404
I'll leave then.

19:15.488 --> 19:17.657
- Yes, go.
- Bye.

19:17.740 --> 19:20.618
- Go. Hurry.
- All right. Bye.

19:22.995 --> 19:24.288
Don't.

19:24.372 --> 19:26.457
Good God.

19:34.090 --> 19:35.341
Go already!

19:40.429 --> 19:42.973
Why did you leave all the lights on?

19:44.141 --> 19:45.935
Money doesn't grow on trees.

19:46.018 --> 19:50.106
You said you'd come tomorrow with Mi-rae.
Why did you show up without calling me?

19:50.189 --> 19:52.900
What would've happened
if we'd missed each other?

19:52.983 --> 19:54.985
Seriously,
what would have happened?

19:55.069 --> 19:56.570
I never would've guessed.

19:56.654 --> 19:58.739
Jeez.

19:59.573 --> 20:01.117
Good Lord.

20:01.617 --> 20:04.995
I can't believe I saw my daughter
kissing a guy in the street.

20:05.079 --> 20:06.247
I'm hungry.

20:07.206 --> 20:09.583
Is there anything to eat?

20:10.876 --> 20:12.169
Didn't you say you ate already?

20:12.253 --> 20:14.714
That was just to get him to leave quickly.

20:14.797 --> 20:16.006
I'm starving.

20:16.507 --> 20:17.967
Order something for me.

20:18.551 --> 20:22.346
We could've just eaten with Ho-su.

20:22.430 --> 20:24.014
What's wrong with you?

20:24.098 --> 20:27.143
You made things so awkward
by cutting him off and sending him away.

20:27.226 --> 20:29.478
You even lied to send him away.

20:30.146 --> 20:31.522
Do you know Ho-su isn't well?

20:32.565 --> 20:33.733
What?

20:35.735 --> 20:37.236
Come and sit down.

20:39.029 --> 20:41.157
His mom told me.

20:41.240 --> 20:44.285
His hearing is getting worse,
so he needs to be hospitalized.

20:44.368 --> 20:46.078
Why are you bringing that up?

20:46.746 --> 20:49.623
Was that the reason you acted that way?

20:49.707 --> 20:53.753
What does his condition have to do
with us seeing each other?

20:53.836 --> 20:58.424
You knew? And you made him
pack boxes this late?

20:58.507 --> 20:59.800
He's about to be hospitalized.

20:59.884 --> 21:03.095
If his mom found out, she'd faint!

21:03.596 --> 21:06.557
I didn't really make him do much.

21:06.640 --> 21:09.852
Do you think it's easy
being with someone who's unwell?

21:10.436 --> 21:13.898
You need to become much more mature
and tougher than you are now.

21:13.981 --> 21:16.859
If you're not ready for that,
don't even start this.

21:16.942 --> 21:21.113
Don't hurt a good kid just because
things get hard later on. Got it?

21:22.656 --> 21:23.908
I won't.

21:24.825 --> 21:26.160
I mean it.

21:26.243 --> 21:28.329
God, what was I thinking?

21:29.330 --> 21:31.582
I can't believe I said
you weren't interested in dating.

21:31.665 --> 21:33.209
Jeez Louise, my head hurts.

21:35.836 --> 21:37.171
Just order some food.

21:54.063 --> 21:56.816
Wow. American chocolate.

22:01.278 --> 22:05.407
Wow, fancy whiskey. It's 30 years old.

22:05.491 --> 22:06.700
Wow…

22:10.704 --> 22:12.998
What are you sharpening?
It's kind of scary.

22:13.082 --> 22:14.375
Just say it.

22:14.875 --> 22:16.710
- Say what?
- Anything.

22:17.253 --> 22:19.713
All I have after studying abroad
is a high school diploma.

22:19.797 --> 22:20.798
Just yell at me already.

22:21.799 --> 22:23.884
Why would I yell at you for that?

22:26.011 --> 22:28.764
Because I didn't see it through
to the end.

22:30.516 --> 22:33.310
You worked so hard to support me.

22:36.105 --> 22:37.606
Is graduation "the end"?

22:39.149 --> 22:42.236
People get a college diploma
to help them start working.

22:43.320 --> 22:45.030
You said you're starting work now.

22:45.739 --> 22:47.449
So, you saw it through to the end.

22:49.118 --> 22:50.119
Still…

22:51.954 --> 22:54.415
You don't stay on the bus
until the last stop.

22:55.457 --> 22:57.001
You get off when it's your stop.

22:58.085 --> 22:59.086
And…

23:00.129 --> 23:01.672
why is the end so important?

23:02.798 --> 23:04.425
The beginning is what matters.

23:07.011 --> 23:10.055
Wow, you're quite talkative today.

23:13.517 --> 23:15.728
Should we open
the 30-year-old whiskey today?

23:27.364 --> 23:30.826
I told him not to save it for too long.
He never even drank it.

23:51.055 --> 23:52.014
It's nice.

23:53.474 --> 23:56.602
Mi-rae said she's meeting someone
and will be here around lunchtime.

23:56.685 --> 23:58.354
I'm going to the real estate office.

23:58.437 --> 23:59.897
Hey, Mi-ji.

24:00.689 --> 24:03.484
Wait for me. Let's go together.

24:04.234 --> 24:06.320
- Together?
- Yes.

24:06.403 --> 24:08.781
Didn't you come to help Mi-rae move?

24:09.406 --> 24:11.492
There's barely anything to help with.

24:12.701 --> 24:15.621
I came because you said
you were signing a lease.

24:16.288 --> 24:17.414
Let's go.

24:18.916 --> 24:20.167
Look who's being nice.

24:20.709 --> 24:22.378
What do you mean?

24:22.461 --> 24:23.462
Let's go.

24:23.963 --> 24:25.506
Move, hurry.

24:27.800 --> 24:30.386
How did you manage to find time
during lunch?

24:31.220 --> 24:33.138
I'm quitting soon, so it doesn't matter.

24:35.391 --> 24:37.768
So, what happened to everyone?

24:38.394 --> 24:42.106
Maybe it's because of the media coverage,
but it wrapped up sooner than expected.

24:47.861 --> 24:50.906
Mr. Shin was the first
to be fired as a scapegoat.

24:53.117 --> 24:54.660
And Director Choi,

24:55.452 --> 24:57.413
who is a department head now…

24:57.496 --> 24:58.872
PLACE OF ASSIGNMENT: CHILDAL BRANCH

24:58.956 --> 25:01.083
…got transferred to the Childal branch.

25:01.166 --> 25:03.794
He was rumored to be moving
to Sihan Construction.

25:03.877 --> 25:07.381
But I guess things didn't work out,
so he's just going to Childal.

25:09.925 --> 25:11.176
And my sister…

25:12.177 --> 25:13.429
came out of her room.

25:15.472 --> 25:17.391
She still has trouble going out,

25:18.308 --> 25:20.352
but she's started therapy too.

25:22.104 --> 25:23.647
It's all thanks to you.

25:27.526 --> 25:28.569
What about you, Tae-i?

25:29.570 --> 25:32.031
Now that things with your sister
are settled,

25:32.114 --> 25:33.365
are you going back to school?

25:34.158 --> 25:35.367
I thought about it,

25:36.118 --> 25:38.287
but I've decided to spend time
with my sister

25:38.370 --> 25:39.663
and start looking for a job.

25:40.581 --> 25:42.958
Turns out, office life suits me
more than I expected.

25:44.710 --> 25:48.088
What? Why do you think that?

25:48.172 --> 25:50.049
Working in an office
is easier than grad school.

25:50.132 --> 25:52.509
- What?
- I get off work on time,

25:52.593 --> 25:53.761
and there are no professors.

25:55.596 --> 25:57.097
So what will you do?

25:58.348 --> 25:59.641
Farming.

26:00.893 --> 26:01.894
What?

26:02.770 --> 26:06.523
Can you give me some context?

26:08.358 --> 26:10.319
The water seems to be running fine.

26:11.153 --> 26:13.155
- Is this a storage space?
- I've checked everything.

26:13.238 --> 26:15.699
I looked at more than ten places
before choosing this place!

26:15.783 --> 26:17.659
Okay. Stay out of this.

26:17.743 --> 26:20.704
Your mom is really thorough.

26:20.788 --> 26:23.582
But honestly,
there's no better place than this one.

26:23.665 --> 26:26.877
Today alone,
five people came by to see it.

26:26.960 --> 26:29.671
Why didn't any of them sign the lease?

26:29.755 --> 26:32.508
- Because your daughter reserved it first.
- I see.

26:32.591 --> 26:34.676
Everyone's waiting for this
to be available again.

26:34.760 --> 26:37.012
- Mom.
- Goodness.

26:37.096 --> 26:39.098
I told you to stay out of this.

26:39.181 --> 26:42.017
It's not bad, but it's a bit too small.

26:42.726 --> 26:45.229
I heard there's a unit
with a living room too.

26:45.312 --> 26:46.730
How much is the rent?

26:46.814 --> 26:49.650
The ones with living rooms
are a bit pricier.

26:55.489 --> 26:58.117
Everyone starts out in a studio.

26:58.200 --> 27:00.828
If you start out in a big place,

27:00.911 --> 27:03.372
you won't be able to keep up
with the costs later.

27:04.957 --> 27:06.959
Lastly, please check

27:07.042 --> 27:08.669
- the real estate registry record.
- Okay.

27:08.752 --> 27:10.838
If it looks good,
we can proceed with the contract.

27:10.921 --> 27:11.922
All right.

27:13.423 --> 27:14.466
Well…

27:15.592 --> 27:17.469
I don't see a problem.

27:17.553 --> 27:19.221
Excuse me, but…

27:19.763 --> 27:23.976
If I put down a bit more for the deposit,
can we lower the monthly rent

27:24.059 --> 27:25.435
by about 50,000 won?

27:26.145 --> 27:28.397
I'll ask the landlord.

27:31.024 --> 27:33.861
Mom, I can't put down any more
for the deposit.

27:35.279 --> 27:36.738
Who said you had to?

27:37.489 --> 27:39.575
I'm using the money
from my matured savings.

27:40.659 --> 27:42.494
Just pay me back when you move out.

27:43.412 --> 27:44.496
Okay.

27:45.539 --> 27:47.082
- The landlord agreed.
- Really?

27:49.042 --> 27:50.210
Thank you.

27:52.713 --> 27:57.551
Now write your name under "Tenant,"
and sign here. On both forms.

27:57.634 --> 27:58.760
All right.

28:02.389 --> 28:04.933
What are you doing? Sign here.

28:05.475 --> 28:06.560
Me?

28:06.643 --> 28:09.062
Of course. It's your place.
Who else would sign?

28:09.146 --> 28:10.314
Right.

28:11.106 --> 28:12.399
Here.

28:15.360 --> 28:17.070
I said sign!

28:17.154 --> 28:20.449
What's with your handwriting?
Are you in elementary school?

28:20.532 --> 28:22.409
It's my first time signing something.

28:23.744 --> 28:26.413
Let's get a stamp made for you later.

28:26.496 --> 28:28.832
TENANT: YU MI-JI

28:29.458 --> 28:30.584
There.

28:33.587 --> 28:36.715
Hello, this is the teachers' office
at Duson Elementary School.

28:40.344 --> 28:42.512
Yes, this is she. Did you say flowers?

28:43.388 --> 28:44.723
Who are they from?

28:46.516 --> 28:47.643
Hello?

28:52.689 --> 28:53.815
Mom.

28:54.316 --> 28:56.485
Oh my, what's gotten into you?

28:57.027 --> 28:58.487
Goodness me.

28:58.570 --> 29:02.532
Gosh. You could've called me.

29:02.616 --> 29:04.284
This is my son.

29:04.368 --> 29:07.871
So you're the lawyer son
we've heard so much about?

29:07.955 --> 29:09.456
- Hello.
- Right.

29:09.539 --> 29:10.791
Hello.

29:10.874 --> 29:13.001
What is all this? My goodness!

29:13.085 --> 29:14.253
What's this for?

29:14.878 --> 29:17.047
- I didn't want to come empty-handed.
- Gosh.

29:17.130 --> 29:18.674
He really is handsome.

29:18.757 --> 29:20.259
I know he is.

29:23.178 --> 29:26.139
You didn't have to come.
There's nothing special to see.

29:26.223 --> 29:29.601
My plans got canceled,
so I wanted to visit you at work.

29:30.435 --> 29:32.229
Anything new with you lately?

29:32.312 --> 29:33.355
Nothing special.

29:35.023 --> 29:37.651
Did you know Mi-rae
quit her job and moved here?

29:38.694 --> 29:41.321
She's going to run a strawberry farm now.

29:42.739 --> 29:45.284
And the owner of that farm…

29:46.493 --> 29:48.578
was the same one Mi-ji had a thing with

29:49.371 --> 29:50.289
What?

29:50.372 --> 29:51.373
You know.

29:51.957 --> 29:54.084
Mi-ji and the farm owner…

29:55.085 --> 29:56.503
liked each other.

29:59.798 --> 30:01.258
I don't think that's true.

30:01.341 --> 30:02.634
It is!

30:03.176 --> 30:04.511
Lots of people saw them.

30:05.262 --> 30:07.472
People said Gyeong-gu and the farm owner

30:07.556 --> 30:11.018
got into a fight over Mi-ji
and ended up rolling on the ground.

30:13.854 --> 30:16.732
Actually, we're seeing each other.

30:17.357 --> 30:18.442
Who?

30:19.484 --> 30:20.694
The farm owner?

30:20.777 --> 30:24.448
No, not him. Mi-ji.

30:26.491 --> 30:28.035
I'm dating Mi-ji.

30:28.577 --> 30:31.747
Mi-ji? But you two
have hardly spent any time together.

30:33.248 --> 30:35.167
Is that why Mi-ji went to Seoul?

30:35.250 --> 30:36.960
No, it's not that.

30:38.003 --> 30:41.089
I've liked her for a long time.

30:41.840 --> 30:42.966
Since high school.

30:45.385 --> 30:49.097
All this time I thought it was Mi-rae.

30:50.557 --> 30:51.808
It was Mi-ji?

30:53.852 --> 30:56.521
You know how I was
when we first moved here.

30:57.105 --> 30:58.732
I was on edge and prickly.

30:59.941 --> 31:02.694
Thanks to Mi-ji, I've changed a lot.

31:04.112 --> 31:06.782
When I'm with her, I laugh a lot more.

31:09.451 --> 31:13.705
Honestly, Mi-ji's the best there is.

31:13.789 --> 31:16.291
I would know because I've worked with her.

31:16.375 --> 31:18.919
But you said that, unlike Mi-rae,
Mi-ji still seems like a kid.

31:19.002 --> 31:21.922
I was saying she's pure-hearted.
And bubbly.

31:23.173 --> 31:25.217
She's just pure.

31:26.426 --> 31:29.471
I'm happy for you, Ho-su. Congratulations.

31:33.183 --> 31:35.435
My son is dating now.

31:38.522 --> 31:41.274
You've never had pho before?
Not even once?

31:42.275 --> 31:44.111
I've had it in school lunches.

31:45.237 --> 31:47.697
But that was more like beef bone soup.

31:48.657 --> 31:51.952
This one smells and tastes
totally different. It's pretty good.

31:52.786 --> 31:55.622
You should go out
and eat good food sometimes.

31:55.705 --> 31:58.500
And didn't your old classmates
go to Vietnam or somewhere?

31:58.583 --> 32:00.419
You should join them on trips like that.

32:00.502 --> 32:02.421
You should be the one
going out and having fun.

32:02.504 --> 32:04.631
Go abroad like everyone else.

32:05.507 --> 32:07.175
Isn't there anywhere you want to go?

32:07.259 --> 32:08.552
Not really.

32:10.262 --> 32:11.721
You're the same, Mom.

32:11.805 --> 32:15.934
Hey, I wanted to travel the world
at your age.

32:16.726 --> 32:18.395
That's why I married your dad.

32:18.478 --> 32:22.023
He said if I went with him to France
for his expat posting, I could study art.

32:22.107 --> 32:25.402
That darn Louvre
and the Musée d'Orsay had me fooled.

32:26.528 --> 32:30.073
But then you two came along
and the IMF crisis hit,

32:30.699 --> 32:32.617
and I never even got a stamp
in my passport.

32:33.869 --> 32:35.620
You wanted to study art?

32:36.121 --> 32:37.664
Didn't I tell you?

32:38.915 --> 32:40.834
I was going to go to art school,

32:40.917 --> 32:43.128
but your grandma was against it,
so I moved to Seoul.

32:43.211 --> 32:45.046
I told her I'd pay for my tuition.

32:46.631 --> 32:48.216
I still remember going around

32:48.300 --> 32:51.011
looking for a place to live
when I first came to Seoul.

32:51.803 --> 32:55.140
Because I was a young girl on my own,
people looked down on me

32:55.223 --> 32:57.309
and only showed me unlivable places.

32:57.392 --> 32:59.436
Those awful people.

33:01.521 --> 33:04.357
Did you come because you were worried
I'd go through the same thing?

33:04.441 --> 33:06.401
Did you think I came to see the sights?

33:09.905 --> 33:11.031
Gosh.

33:11.114 --> 33:15.952
It's nice to be back in Seoul
after so long.

33:18.580 --> 33:20.040
It's nice to eat this too.

33:22.334 --> 33:23.877
Couldn't you still do it?

33:23.960 --> 33:25.170
Do what?

33:26.254 --> 33:28.173
What you always wanted.

33:28.256 --> 33:29.799
You can still paint, right?

33:29.883 --> 33:32.260
Come on, it's too late for me…

33:32.802 --> 33:35.639
You should do what you want,
now that you're in Seoul.

33:36.473 --> 33:37.849
It's too late for me.

33:37.933 --> 33:39.392
We're not the same…

33:45.440 --> 33:46.942
Fine, I'll paint.

33:48.276 --> 33:50.111
So you should do what you want too.

33:51.196 --> 33:54.407
As long as it's not a crime,
I won't stop you.

33:54.491 --> 33:57.410
Right, you even let Mi-rae farm.

33:57.953 --> 33:58.828
Jeez.

33:59.829 --> 34:02.249
I won't stop you. Really.

34:06.545 --> 34:09.089
I would've been fine on my own.
You didn't have to come.

34:09.172 --> 34:10.382
What time is it?

34:10.465 --> 34:11.675
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

34:11.758 --> 34:13.635
- Go straight home.
- Got it.

34:13.718 --> 34:15.554
- All right.
- Call me when you get home.

34:15.637 --> 34:17.722
- Go already.
- Okay.

34:19.015 --> 34:20.100
Mom.

34:25.522 --> 34:26.731
Thank you.

34:28.066 --> 34:29.109
For what?

34:29.818 --> 34:30.860
Everything.

34:31.486 --> 34:32.612
Jeez.

34:32.696 --> 34:35.574
What's with you? You're being all mushy.

34:37.033 --> 34:40.036
Just go already. Go!

34:41.121 --> 34:42.122
Go, hurry!

34:42.205 --> 34:44.040
Okay. You go first.

34:44.666 --> 34:45.667
Go.

34:47.168 --> 34:49.838
- Jeez. Go.
- I will.

34:52.007 --> 34:53.425
Seriously, go!

34:53.508 --> 34:55.260
I am going!

34:57.012 --> 34:58.888
- I'll call you.
- All right.

35:02.559 --> 35:03.768
Hey! Yu Mi-rae!

35:08.106 --> 35:09.816
Do you have to go this far?

35:10.400 --> 35:12.444
Do we really need
to take this to civil court?

35:12.527 --> 35:14.404
Isn't it enough that I quit?

35:14.487 --> 35:17.699
You quit because
you were afraid you'd get fired.

35:18.617 --> 35:21.286
I got a suspended sentence.
What more do you want?

35:21.369 --> 35:22.996
I've already paid the price.

35:23.788 --> 35:26.791
That was just your share
of the consequences.

35:29.210 --> 35:32.881
Breaking a window and owning up to it
doesn't magically replace the glass.

35:33.965 --> 35:36.801
You still have to compensate
for the damage you caused.

35:36.885 --> 35:39.137
How much more do I have to suffer
before you're satisfied?

35:39.220 --> 35:41.640
Well, you should pay the interest too.

35:51.483 --> 35:53.526
Should I file for a restraining order too?

35:54.235 --> 35:56.404
I'm pretty sure
he'd like to file one against me.

35:57.405 --> 36:00.158
I heard you were busy,
but you always come in person.

36:00.659 --> 36:01.951
Thank you.

36:02.702 --> 36:04.829
I should fix the mess I started.

36:05.997 --> 36:08.958
Would you like me to drop you off
somewhere on the way?

36:09.042 --> 36:11.711
No, I have somewhere to go. Bye.

36:27.936 --> 36:29.813
Why do I feel lonely?

36:29.896 --> 36:31.439
No one's coming anyway.

36:32.565 --> 36:34.484
Let's just hit up the duty-free shops.

36:46.496 --> 36:48.540
Where are you right now?

36:49.082 --> 36:50.834
I'm at the airport.

36:51.459 --> 36:52.836
The airport?

36:53.670 --> 36:55.463
I'm already inside.

36:58.842 --> 37:00.009
Already?

37:00.093 --> 37:02.220
You should've told me you were coming.

37:02.303 --> 37:04.764
I asked you more than five times,
and you said no.

37:05.265 --> 37:08.518
I wasn't sure when I'd be done.

37:08.601 --> 37:11.020
Then you could've told me when you left.

37:11.104 --> 37:13.523
Is it that hard to send a text
saying you're coming?

37:13.606 --> 37:15.191
No wonder I didn't want
to go inside.

37:16.735 --> 37:17.736
I…

37:19.028 --> 37:21.239
I wanted to tell you in person.

37:22.407 --> 37:23.366
Thank you…

37:24.159 --> 37:26.536
for everything, really.

37:27.662 --> 37:28.955
Have a safe trip--

37:29.038 --> 37:30.206
Ms. Yu Mi-rae!

37:37.338 --> 37:40.091
You said you had gone in already…

37:40.175 --> 37:43.511
The check-in area. For first class.

37:43.595 --> 37:45.847
I was checking in when you called.

37:45.930 --> 37:48.808
You could've said that
instead of running over.

37:50.560 --> 37:52.020
I was worried you'd leave.

37:52.103 --> 37:55.106
You're impatient.
I figured you'd disappear again.

38:01.613 --> 38:02.906
So what now?

38:03.907 --> 38:07.702
It's not too late.
Should I get you a ticket?

38:08.495 --> 38:09.662
Please…

38:10.455 --> 38:13.082
ask me again another time.

38:17.128 --> 38:19.547
Don't forget you said you'd send letters.

38:19.631 --> 38:22.967
I said farm updates, not letters…

38:23.051 --> 38:24.052
Whatever.

38:24.135 --> 38:26.221
Newsletters, spam…

38:26.721 --> 38:28.181
Just send anything.

38:29.682 --> 38:30.892
Promise?

38:41.611 --> 38:44.697
By the way, we can hug, right?

38:46.533 --> 38:48.243
Sure. Why not?

38:57.627 --> 38:59.295
If you come back to Korea,

39:00.171 --> 39:02.507
you're always welcome at home.

39:04.008 --> 39:05.093
I'll be back.

39:13.184 --> 39:14.310
Darn it.

39:20.108 --> 39:22.902
It must be tough to stay
in the hospital for a whole week.

39:22.986 --> 39:25.530
I wish I could do this for you.

39:26.573 --> 39:27.782
Should I pretend to be you?

39:27.866 --> 39:30.535
I got my blood drawn once,
pretending I was Mi-rae.

39:32.036 --> 39:35.623
I can't really talk on the phone,
but I can still text.

39:35.707 --> 39:38.835
Feel free to text me anytime.
I'll be so bored here.

39:39.586 --> 39:41.421
You're going to regret saying that.

39:41.504 --> 39:44.340
I'll show you how loud I can be over text.

39:47.635 --> 39:48.678
Hi, Mi-ji!

39:49.721 --> 39:50.722
Gosh, ma'am!

39:51.681 --> 39:53.433
I happened to be at the hospital…

39:53.975 --> 39:56.436
Wow, what a coincidence!

39:56.519 --> 39:58.813
So what's wrong, exactly?

40:00.440 --> 40:01.733
She knows.

40:02.275 --> 40:04.277
- What?
- Yes. I know.

40:07.113 --> 40:08.990
Stay a little longer.

40:09.490 --> 40:12.660
Don't leave because of me.
Should I just go?

40:12.744 --> 40:13.745
No, don't.

40:13.828 --> 40:16.497
I was just planning to stay
until he got checked in.

40:18.917 --> 40:22.503
You two used to bicker all the time,
and now you've grown up and…

40:24.797 --> 40:28.176
This might seem sudden,

40:29.177 --> 40:32.931
but honestly,
I always felt closer to you, Mi-ji.

40:34.349 --> 40:35.683
I mean it.

40:35.767 --> 40:38.978
Especially on the day
we made strawberry jam together.

40:39.062 --> 40:41.439
I felt it in my gut that day.

40:41.522 --> 40:43.983
Oh, the strawberry jam?

40:50.657 --> 40:54.077
Thank you for being there for Ho-su.

40:55.536 --> 40:58.873
I hope you two make each other happy
for a long, long time.

41:00.208 --> 41:01.793
- Okay.
- Good.

41:03.670 --> 41:06.297
- I'll get going now.
- All right.

41:07.090 --> 41:08.049
- Bye.
- Okay.

41:08.132 --> 41:09.634
- Bye.
- Bye.

41:12.512 --> 41:14.514
- Bye.
- Go.

41:17.225 --> 41:18.851
- Take care.
- All right.

41:32.490 --> 41:33.491
Hi, Mom.

41:35.368 --> 41:36.744
Why do you sound like that?

41:38.788 --> 41:40.248
What's wrong with Grandma?

41:41.708 --> 41:42.750
What?

41:48.172 --> 41:49.674
VACANT

41:49.757 --> 41:52.301
Sir, please go to Seoul Station.

41:53.302 --> 41:55.304
BONGDEOK HOSPITAL

41:59.100 --> 42:00.727
Mom, where's Grandma?

42:01.269 --> 42:03.354
You're here. She's inside.

42:03.980 --> 42:06.274
Mi-rae's on her way. Sit.

42:08.568 --> 42:09.902
What happened?

42:10.445 --> 42:11.821
A heart attack?

42:11.904 --> 42:13.489
Is she okay now?

42:16.451 --> 42:19.662
Then why did you bring her back
to the nursing home?

42:19.746 --> 42:22.123
She should've stayed in the ER.

42:22.206 --> 42:25.168
They said there's nothing more
they can do for her here either.

42:25.251 --> 42:27.837
She's old and very weak,

42:27.920 --> 42:30.048
so she might not make it
through treatment.

42:30.673 --> 42:31.716
What?

42:32.216 --> 42:34.677
So we just leave her like this?

42:34.761 --> 42:37.597
Mom, let's try another hospital.

42:41.559 --> 42:44.437
- We're taking her home.
- What?

42:44.520 --> 42:47.815
She's been saying
she wants to go home for days.

42:48.357 --> 42:49.776
We'll bring her home.

42:50.359 --> 42:53.321
You said she might not make it
past a few days.

42:53.946 --> 42:56.532
We have to do everything we can.
Why are we giving up?

42:56.616 --> 42:57.575
Mom.

42:58.076 --> 42:59.619
Let's go.

42:59.702 --> 43:01.412
Let's try one more hospital.

43:01.496 --> 43:03.664
Do you think I want this?

43:09.378 --> 43:11.214
She wants to go home.

43:12.256 --> 43:14.801
That's all we can do for her now.

43:33.402 --> 43:34.821
I should've come yesterday.

43:35.905 --> 43:37.323
Or the day before.

43:39.325 --> 43:41.786
Why did I listen
when she said not to come?

43:48.459 --> 43:49.544
Grandma.

43:50.044 --> 43:52.797
Are you with me? It's me, Mi-ji.

43:53.840 --> 43:54.799
Mi-ji.

43:55.424 --> 43:56.551
Yes.

43:57.885 --> 43:59.011
Let's go.

43:59.095 --> 44:01.389
What? What was that?

44:05.268 --> 44:06.561
Home.

44:09.355 --> 44:12.942
I want to go home.

44:17.613 --> 44:18.614
Okay.

44:20.825 --> 44:22.368
Let's go home now.

44:23.578 --> 44:25.288
Grandma, we'll go home.

44:27.415 --> 44:28.541
Let's go.

44:31.294 --> 44:32.837
Let's go home, Grandma.

45:25.431 --> 45:27.266
Mom's completely out.

45:28.017 --> 45:30.228
She probably hasn't slept in days.

45:31.020 --> 45:33.898
This reminds me of the old days.

45:35.233 --> 45:38.319
Grandma never fell asleep before we did.

45:39.153 --> 45:40.821
You should get some sleep too.

45:40.905 --> 45:43.241
You haven't slept
since you got here yesterday.

45:43.991 --> 45:45.117
I'm good.

45:55.419 --> 45:56.671
Hey.

45:56.754 --> 45:59.090
How are things at the farm?

45:59.173 --> 46:02.176
Things are fine for now, but who knows.

46:03.094 --> 46:05.680
Are you sure you don't want
to work with me?

46:06.597 --> 46:07.932
I'll pay you.

46:08.432 --> 46:10.935
How much?
Will you pay me 200,000 won a day?

46:11.018 --> 46:14.647
The best part of having a sister
is cheap labor.

46:14.730 --> 46:16.023
Goodness.

46:16.691 --> 46:18.818
Look how shameless you've become.

46:19.527 --> 46:22.154
It's too much for me
to handle alone right now.

46:22.238 --> 46:24.323
Can't you help a few days a week?

46:24.407 --> 46:27.743
I could probably help out
for a day here and there.

46:28.286 --> 46:30.621
Why? Did you already get a job?

46:32.039 --> 46:34.500
What is it? Why can't you tell me?

46:35.584 --> 46:37.420
Wait, are you getting married?

46:37.503 --> 46:39.547
Hey, are you crazy?

46:39.630 --> 46:41.590
How could I get married?

46:41.674 --> 46:44.802
If you're not getting married,
what are you trying to hide?

46:45.761 --> 46:48.014
Stop dragging it out and just tell me.

46:48.597 --> 46:49.765
What is it?

46:50.349 --> 46:51.559
It's just…

46:52.893 --> 46:55.646
I was thinking of… going to college.

46:56.272 --> 46:57.565
What?

46:57.648 --> 46:59.066
Cabbage? What do you mean?

46:59.567 --> 47:01.902
I said "college."

47:02.903 --> 47:04.405
College!

47:04.488 --> 47:06.324
The one you take the CSAT for!

47:06.407 --> 47:08.117
You?

47:08.200 --> 47:10.703
I mean, there's no need…

47:12.788 --> 47:17.043
I've been to college,
and honestly, you don't need it.

47:17.126 --> 47:18.085
You might be better off

47:18.169 --> 47:20.796
doing something else
instead of studying for the CSAT.

47:20.880 --> 47:21.881
I know.

47:21.964 --> 47:24.842
Having a degree
doesn't guarantee anything.

47:24.925 --> 47:27.595
And I know wanting to go
doesn't mean I can.

47:28.429 --> 47:29.472
But…

47:30.014 --> 47:31.057
I'm embarrassed.

47:31.140 --> 47:32.058
About what?

47:33.434 --> 47:35.394
Ever since I was little,

47:35.478 --> 47:38.481
I knew I could never catch up to you,
no matter how hard I tried.

47:38.564 --> 47:40.441
So I gave up on studying early.

47:41.067 --> 47:45.029
I figured it was less embarrassing
to not try than to fail.

47:46.947 --> 47:47.990
But…

47:48.616 --> 47:51.202
now I'm not sure
if that's really less embarrassing.

47:53.537 --> 47:55.915
When I filled in for you at KFMC,

47:55.998 --> 47:58.376
I was terrified at first.

47:58.959 --> 48:01.670
I couldn't follow what anyone was saying,

48:01.754 --> 48:04.965
and everyone was so smart
that I was scared to even talk to them.

48:05.466 --> 48:08.886
But I had to report to the boss,
so I studied a bit

48:08.969 --> 48:10.471
and started to understand things.

48:10.554 --> 48:14.058
It all sounded complicated,
but there was nothing to be nervous about.

48:14.141 --> 48:17.561
After that, I wasn't scared anymore.

48:18.521 --> 48:20.773
Maybe college is like that too.

48:21.524 --> 48:23.734
The thing I'm most scared
and embarrassed of.

48:26.278 --> 48:27.571
I want to try it.

48:30.408 --> 48:31.534
You're right.

48:32.493 --> 48:34.161
Things might seem scary,

48:34.245 --> 48:36.539
but once you dive in,
they're not all that.

48:37.248 --> 48:40.626
College might disappoint you too. But…

48:41.710 --> 48:43.963
it's better to try and be disappointed.

48:44.046 --> 48:45.464
I'm all for it.

48:46.424 --> 48:48.509
- Man.
- But…

48:49.051 --> 48:51.220
if you want to go to college,

48:51.303 --> 48:53.472
you'll have to study like hell.

48:54.390 --> 48:56.475
Even if Ho-su tutors you…

48:58.227 --> 48:59.311
Anyways,

48:59.895 --> 49:01.689
you'll have to work your butt off.

49:01.772 --> 49:04.525
Hey, why are you scaring me already?

49:05.568 --> 49:07.778
Have you picked your major? Never mind.

49:07.862 --> 49:10.156
Just go wherever your grades take you.

49:10.239 --> 49:11.991
Grandma, did you hear her?

49:12.074 --> 49:14.535
She's looking down on me
just because she's smart.

49:14.618 --> 49:16.328
I'm not looking down on you.

49:16.871 --> 49:18.372
You'll have to work really hard.

49:18.456 --> 49:20.708
Don't you dare look down on me.
I'll bust my butt.

49:20.791 --> 49:22.460
Should I take the exam for you?

49:22.543 --> 49:24.378
Really? Should we switch again?

49:24.462 --> 49:27.089
See, that's your problem right there.

49:27.173 --> 49:28.966
Gosh, are you messing with me?

49:29.049 --> 49:30.551
Even with my eyes wide open…

49:30.634 --> 49:33.179
"Even with my eyes

49:33.262 --> 49:36.307
wide open…"

49:36.390 --> 49:37.933
…the dream stays the same.

49:38.017 --> 49:39.852
"…the dream

49:40.519 --> 49:45.524
stays the same."

49:47.735 --> 49:51.614
"The dream stays the same."

49:52.531 --> 49:56.118
Is there something you'd like
to read once your dyslexia improves?

49:56.202 --> 49:59.413
There is one thing I want to read.

50:00.039 --> 50:02.458
But I don't know what it says.

50:04.376 --> 50:05.503
Should I read it for you?

50:06.128 --> 50:07.129
No.

50:09.131 --> 50:11.342
What if it says something bad about me?

50:26.815 --> 50:32.071
KIM RO-SA

50:42.831 --> 50:46.585
"My world…

50:47.795 --> 50:50.673
began to sing…"

50:52.841 --> 50:54.343
- "Sangwol."
- "My world…"

50:54.426 --> 50:55.761
"A term for frost and the moon."

50:55.844 --> 50:59.306
"…began to sing after meeting you.

51:00.307 --> 51:02.268
Just as the wind carries the bird,

51:03.477 --> 51:06.438
you led me to poetry.

51:08.440 --> 51:09.608
My song,

51:10.859 --> 51:12.236
my wind…"

51:15.990 --> 51:17.700
"My…

51:22.454 --> 51:24.957
Sang… wol."

51:26.208 --> 51:29.420
MY SONG, MY WIND
MY SANG-WOL

51:37.845 --> 51:40.973
"Dawn Rain."

51:42.516 --> 51:44.768
INTERPRETATION OF SLEEP

52:04.330 --> 52:05.414
Grandma.

52:11.629 --> 52:12.880
Grandma.

52:17.259 --> 52:18.302
Grandma!

52:18.385 --> 52:19.386
You startled me.

52:19.470 --> 52:22.306
Why are you up already?
You should sleep some more.

52:22.389 --> 52:25.309
What happened? Are you all better now?

52:25.392 --> 52:26.393
Of course.

52:26.935 --> 52:29.438
Lying down all day was exhausting.

52:29.521 --> 52:30.773
Thank goodness.

52:30.856 --> 52:33.984
I was worried something serious
might happen to you.

52:34.693 --> 52:35.778
What are you doing?

52:35.861 --> 52:36.862
Packing.

52:37.738 --> 52:39.907
All of a sudden? Are you going somewhere?

52:40.407 --> 52:42.409
I've been lying in bed for ten years.

52:42.493 --> 52:44.453
It's time I got out and about.

52:44.536 --> 52:47.164
When the flowers bloom,
I'll go to Jeju Island.

52:47.247 --> 52:49.541
When the snow melts,
I'll hike Mount Seorak.

52:50.167 --> 52:53.462
Maybe I'll even travel abroad for once.

52:53.545 --> 52:54.922
I want to come too.

52:55.005 --> 52:56.924
You need to go to college.

52:57.007 --> 53:00.511
Didn't you hear what Mi-rae said?
You have to study hard to get in.

53:01.887 --> 53:04.056
Then I won't go to college.

53:04.139 --> 53:06.100
I'll just travel and have fun with you!

53:06.767 --> 53:07.851
Have fun later.

53:08.352 --> 53:11.438
You've got so much to do,
and all you think about is having fun.

53:14.650 --> 53:16.527
Why are you going that way?

53:16.610 --> 53:19.613
Have you been gone so long
that you forgot where the door is?

53:23.492 --> 53:24.702
It doesn't matter.

53:25.369 --> 53:27.329
It's not like I'll be walking.

53:43.303 --> 53:44.513
Grandma.

53:47.683 --> 53:48.809
Don't go.

53:50.018 --> 53:52.062
Stay with me.

53:55.357 --> 53:57.484
Why are you acting like a baby again?

53:59.361 --> 54:01.572
I know you won't come back if you leave.

54:03.490 --> 54:05.451
No, I'm not letting you go.

54:09.455 --> 54:11.832
I'll always come back.

54:12.416 --> 54:14.251
On your hard days,

54:15.377 --> 54:17.171
I'll come to you as a cloud

54:17.921 --> 54:19.840
or as a bird.

54:21.550 --> 54:24.136
What if I don't recognize you?

54:24.803 --> 54:27.347
I won't know if it's you.

54:28.849 --> 54:30.267
Of course you'll know.

54:30.934 --> 54:33.604
If you see a funny-shaped cloud

54:34.438 --> 54:36.690
or a bird staring right at you,

54:37.357 --> 54:38.859
you'll know it's me.

54:41.361 --> 54:43.363
You'll know right away, Mi-ji.

54:44.990 --> 54:46.909
It's nothing to be sad about.

54:47.618 --> 54:50.829
You don't need to come to the hospital.
I'll always be with you.

54:52.748 --> 54:56.752
I want to see your place in Seoul,
since I couldn't when I was bedridden.

54:57.419 --> 55:01.715
I also want to see
the college you'll get into.

55:04.635 --> 55:06.929
Grandma, was it hard for you?

55:08.931 --> 55:10.849
Were you in pain and frustrated?

55:14.144 --> 55:15.270
Mi-ji.

55:16.814 --> 55:18.398
If you can't stop crying,

55:19.650 --> 55:22.778
and if you feel so sad and lost
that you can't do anything,

55:24.029 --> 55:26.365
then I'll stay a little longer.

55:27.866 --> 55:29.076
Grandma…

55:30.118 --> 55:32.579
can hold on as long as you need me to.

55:49.805 --> 55:51.223
You can go.

55:52.891 --> 55:56.520
I won't cry too much.
I'll live my life as best as I can.

55:58.021 --> 56:00.440
So don't worry about me.

56:02.401 --> 56:04.444
See the things you wanted to see,

56:04.987 --> 56:08.323
and go to all the places
you wanted to visit.

56:09.825 --> 56:11.535
And every once in a while,

56:13.120 --> 56:14.454
come…

56:15.873 --> 56:17.040
visit me too.

57:18.143 --> 57:19.811
Goodbye, Grandma.

57:23.649 --> 57:24.842
I love you.

57:34.576 --> 57:35.702
Mi-ji.

57:39.581 --> 57:40.666
Mi-ji.

57:46.838 --> 57:48.507
Grandma's gone.

58:05.565 --> 58:07.150
Grandma.

58:32.592 --> 58:33.927
Grandma.

58:57.284 --> 58:59.327
CSAT SPECIAL LECTURE
MATHEMATICS 1

59:01.163 --> 59:02.914
A chapter I loved came to an end.

59:02.998 --> 59:03.957
YU MI-JI

59:04.041 --> 59:05.917
And new days kept coming.

59:07.002 --> 59:08.295
Hello.

59:08.378 --> 59:10.172
Nice to meet you.

59:11.590 --> 59:14.634
In Korean Sign Language,
this is how we clap.

59:15.761 --> 59:18.555
Now, instead of "sign,"

59:18.638 --> 59:20.849
we'll use the term "Korean Sign Language."

59:20.932 --> 59:22.768
Just like Japanese, Chinese, or English…

59:22.851 --> 59:24.352
As always…

59:24.436 --> 59:25.437
Hey, easy.

59:25.520 --> 59:26.396
COMPOUND FERTILIZER

59:26.480 --> 59:29.691
…the days are unfamiliar, new,
and full of uncertainty.

59:31.735 --> 59:34.780
If you use these, it won't be organic.

59:35.864 --> 59:37.532
I'm not doing organic farming.

59:37.616 --> 59:38.784
Really?

59:46.124 --> 59:48.710
Here's today's farm update.

59:48.794 --> 59:51.546
We completed the second round
of fertilizer application.

59:51.630 --> 59:55.383
With the adjusted amount of irrigation,
the leaves are regaining their vitality.

59:56.885 --> 01:00:00.222
The annual yield forecast
is currently being revised upward.

01:00:01.139 --> 01:00:02.015
P.S.

01:00:02.933 --> 01:00:05.769
Everyone came to see the first harvest
of the new strawberry variety.

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:08.480
They were disappointed
and said it was just the same.

01:00:16.154 --> 01:00:18.698
Despite everything,
we still managed to find joy.

01:00:20.117 --> 01:00:22.285
VIEW CSAT SCORE

01:00:28.083 --> 01:00:31.378
GRADE

01:00:35.674 --> 01:00:38.802
Even if the days we push through…

01:00:38.885 --> 01:00:40.262
I blew it.

01:00:40.345 --> 01:00:42.751
- …end on a sour note…
- It's okay, Mi-ji.

01:00:43.640 --> 01:00:48.283
5:00
ALARM

01:00:52.065 --> 01:00:54.484
…a new chapter begins.

01:00:56.153 --> 01:00:58.113
CHEONGSEOL BOARDING PREP ACADEMY

01:00:59.156 --> 01:01:01.116
No need to overthink it.

01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:03.493
You're doing great, okay?

01:01:04.119 --> 01:01:05.704
- Is it sour?
- Yes.

01:01:05.787 --> 01:01:08.373
Jeez, you just watered them wrong.

01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:09.332
Watered them wrong?

01:01:09.416 --> 01:01:13.003
Once a week should be fine.
Yes, that's right.

01:01:16.840 --> 01:01:18.258
THANKS FOR READING

01:01:19.551 --> 01:01:20.427
PUBLISH

01:01:22.429 --> 01:01:23.638
FUTURE-ORIENTED INVESTMENT LOG

01:01:23.722 --> 01:01:25.307
MARKET OUTLOOK AND KEY SECTORS

01:01:25.390 --> 01:01:27.114
GLOBAL TRADE
REGIONALIZATION AND CONTRACTION

01:01:30.187 --> 01:01:31.146
YOU HAVE A NEW COMMENT

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:35.275
I told you. Stocks are your thing.

01:01:35.358 --> 01:01:37.903
Why make life harder by doing farm work?

01:01:40.697 --> 01:01:44.284
Only something even more bitter
can take away the bitterness of farming.

01:01:45.243 --> 01:01:46.828
I hid a potion for you.

01:01:50.874 --> 01:01:53.835
And somehow, we find joy again.

01:01:55.754 --> 01:01:56.880
Ho-su!

01:01:56.963 --> 01:01:58.256
CHEONGSEOL BOARDING PREP ACADEMY

01:01:58.340 --> 01:01:59.216
Mi-ji.

01:01:59.299 --> 01:02:00.467
Oh my!

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:03.553
What did you bring?

01:02:03.637 --> 01:02:04.804
- Fried chicken.
- Nice.

01:02:05.305 --> 01:02:06.598
- Can my friend join?
- And…

01:02:06.681 --> 01:02:08.225
- Of course.
- …we love again.

01:02:09.184 --> 01:02:11.686
Wow, you drew all this yourself?

01:02:11.770 --> 01:02:12.979
Did you take classes?

01:02:13.563 --> 01:02:15.398
Oh please. Not at all.

01:02:15.899 --> 01:02:19.444
Mi-ji! Come out here.
Let's check the results together.

01:02:20.070 --> 01:02:21.780
- It's your third time anyway.
- Sit.

01:02:21.863 --> 01:02:23.573
What's there to hide? Show us.

01:02:23.657 --> 01:02:26.243
No! I want to see it by myself.

01:02:28.578 --> 01:02:30.664
Three, two, one.

01:02:36.127 --> 01:02:39.506
Please, please, please…

01:02:40.131 --> 01:02:42.717
And we reach the last page
of the chapter once more.

01:02:43.510 --> 01:02:44.970
ONE YEAR LATER

01:02:46.638 --> 01:02:48.640
Did you harvest the strawberries?

01:02:48.723 --> 01:02:49.975
- Yes.
- Gosh.

01:02:51.685 --> 01:02:55.605
Hey, Yu Smarty.
Aren't you going to get your cooling vest?

01:02:55.689 --> 01:02:58.191
Can you grab one for me?
I have a meeting with the distributor.

01:02:58.275 --> 01:03:00.235
Wow, a distributor meeting.

01:03:00.318 --> 01:03:03.446
That sounds so fancy.
You're next in line for president.

01:03:04.239 --> 01:03:07.033
Gosh, why does the current president
appoint the next president?

01:03:07.117 --> 01:03:09.536
Shouldn't there be an election first?

01:03:09.619 --> 01:03:11.997
Wait, you've already
harvested your strawberries?

01:03:12.956 --> 01:03:16.001
- It's our second harvest.
- What? Already?

01:03:16.084 --> 01:03:17.711
What's the Brix value?

01:03:17.794 --> 01:03:18.712
Thirteen.

01:03:18.795 --> 01:03:20.547
No way. You're kidding.

01:03:25.468 --> 01:03:27.262
Maybe I should plant these too.

01:03:27.345 --> 01:03:30.181
Jeez. Anyway, get a cooling vest for me.

01:03:31.266 --> 01:03:32.892
I'm heading out now.

01:03:32.976 --> 01:03:34.978
Oh my. These are sweet.

01:03:35.061 --> 01:03:36.521
No settlement today either.

01:03:36.604 --> 01:03:38.773
What if we can't reach
a settlement again next time?

01:03:39.232 --> 01:03:42.777
Then we go to trial. Don't worry.

01:03:42.861 --> 01:03:44.154
Okay.

01:03:46.406 --> 01:03:48.158
The mediation date is in two weeks.

01:03:48.867 --> 01:03:50.410
It's in two weeks.

01:03:50.994 --> 01:03:52.245
In two weeks?

01:03:54.414 --> 01:03:56.124
What was "Great job" again?

01:03:56.624 --> 01:03:58.084
Like this.

01:04:14.726 --> 01:04:16.853
Let's go. Shall we?

01:04:17.687 --> 01:04:19.397
Do you know him?

01:04:19.898 --> 01:04:21.524
He was a junior colleague.

01:04:22.192 --> 01:04:23.193
He's good.

01:04:25.904 --> 01:04:27.489
Excuse me, Senior.

01:04:27.572 --> 01:04:30.742
Do you know when you'll be able
to send the materials you promised?

01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:32.744
I said I'd send them when I'm done.

01:04:32.827 --> 01:04:34.788
If you're in such a hurry, do it yourself.

01:04:34.871 --> 01:04:40.085
But this is a team project,
and I've been doing it all alone…

01:04:40.168 --> 01:04:42.879
Yesterday, you said
you'd send them by the end of the day.

01:04:42.962 --> 01:04:45.298
- So I…
- I told you several times.

01:04:45.382 --> 01:04:47.550
I had Reserve Forces training yesterday.

01:04:47.634 --> 01:04:48.885
Reserve Forces training?

01:04:48.968 --> 01:04:51.554
- What the heck?
- I saw you drinking in the afternoon

01:04:51.638 --> 01:04:53.223
at Grandma's Bar yesterday.

01:04:53.306 --> 01:04:54.516
Why are you butting in?

01:04:54.599 --> 01:04:56.810
I've kept my mouth shut long enough.

01:04:57.477 --> 01:05:00.563
If you have time to lie, copy something
off the Internet and send it.

01:05:00.647 --> 01:05:02.273
You're a senior. Act like one.

01:05:02.357 --> 01:05:03.817
Hey, Junior!

01:05:03.900 --> 01:05:05.318
Just because you're older,

01:05:05.402 --> 01:05:07.195
you think you can talk down
to your seniors?

01:05:07.278 --> 01:05:09.239
Didn't you tell me to drop the honorifics?

01:05:09.322 --> 01:05:10.740
This guy is a nutcase.

01:05:10.824 --> 01:05:13.034
- A nutcase?
- Yes, you psycho.

01:05:13.118 --> 01:05:14.327
Send the file already.

01:05:14.411 --> 01:05:16.204
- You little…
- Don't you dare raise your hand.

01:05:16.287 --> 01:05:18.498
- Who do you think you are?
- I swear I'm going to…

01:05:19.332 --> 01:05:20.917
No, stop fighting!

01:05:21.000 --> 01:05:23.002
- Why are you so strong?
- Please stop!

01:05:23.086 --> 01:05:24.754
- I'm sorry, Mi-ji.
- Stay still!

01:05:27.382 --> 01:05:30.718
I'm sorry I dragged you into that.
It was all because of me.

01:05:30.802 --> 01:05:33.012
Didn't I tell you to stop saying sorry?

01:05:33.513 --> 01:05:35.890
That guy deserved
to get grabbed by the collar,

01:05:35.974 --> 01:05:37.851
but you kept saying "sorry,"

01:05:37.934 --> 01:05:40.019
which made him raise his voice even more.

01:05:40.103 --> 01:05:41.062
Sorry.

01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:45.275
God, what's wrong with me?

01:05:45.358 --> 01:05:48.611
I keep trying to change,

01:05:48.695 --> 01:05:51.656
but it feels like
I always go back to how I was.

01:05:52.282 --> 01:05:53.658
Not at all.

01:05:54.159 --> 01:05:56.619
At the orientation,
you apologized nonstop.

01:05:56.703 --> 01:05:58.204
- Did I?
- Jeez.

01:05:59.080 --> 01:06:02.125
I've got ten more years on you,
so trust me.

01:06:02.750 --> 01:06:05.086
People only move forward.

01:06:05.170 --> 01:06:08.173
You might stumble and fall
or pause for a bit,

01:06:08.256 --> 01:06:10.133
but you never go backward.

01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:13.470
Even if you can't feel it,
you're always moving forward.

01:06:13.553 --> 01:06:15.013
So don't worry.

01:06:15.555 --> 01:06:17.432
- Mi-ji.
- Yes.

01:06:18.183 --> 01:06:20.226
You sounded really old just now.

01:06:20.810 --> 01:06:21.728
Hey.

01:06:21.811 --> 01:06:23.771
"Back to how I was," my foot.

01:06:23.855 --> 01:06:25.648
- Come on.
- Stop bugging your friend.

01:06:25.732 --> 01:06:27.066
Ho-su!

01:06:31.446 --> 01:06:34.782
College kids don't like it
when you talk their ears off.

01:06:35.325 --> 01:06:37.869
I can't help it. My mouth won't stop.

01:06:37.952 --> 01:06:40.788
I can't look the other way
when I see something wrong happening.

01:06:40.872 --> 01:06:41.915
PSYCHOLOGY RESEARCH METHODS

01:06:42.040 --> 01:06:45.251
Why are you the only one
who sees when someone's struggling?

01:06:46.127 --> 01:06:48.796
It's like how you can see
every single strand of hair,

01:06:48.880 --> 01:06:51.424
when I can never see any.
Same thing, I guess.

01:06:53.218 --> 01:06:55.512
I know I should just let it go, but…

01:06:56.137 --> 01:06:58.181
If I have a sense of what's on their mind,

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.141
I just can't let it go.

01:07:01.184 --> 01:07:03.144
Good thing you chose psychology.

01:07:03.228 --> 01:07:06.022
What matters most in psychology
is understanding people's minds,

01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:07.315
which you already do.

01:07:08.066 --> 01:07:11.778
No, statistics and brain structure
matter the most.

01:07:11.861 --> 01:07:13.488
That's…

01:07:14.364 --> 01:07:16.699
You'll do better
when you retake the course.

01:07:16.783 --> 01:07:18.243
Minds matter the most.

01:07:18.326 --> 01:07:19.369
Jeez.

01:07:21.329 --> 01:07:22.372
Let's see.

01:07:23.039 --> 01:07:25.124
What's on your mind…

01:07:25.750 --> 01:07:29.045
You're kind of freaking out
because you think we'll be late.

01:07:29.128 --> 01:07:30.380
- You read that?
- Yes.

01:07:30.463 --> 01:07:31.589
Then let's hurry.

01:07:32.298 --> 01:07:33.967
We're cutting it close with the flowers.

01:07:34.050 --> 01:07:35.009
Right, the flowers!

01:07:35.718 --> 01:07:37.095
Hurry up!

01:07:37.178 --> 01:07:38.680
KIM RO-SA'S POSTHUMOUS POETRY READING

01:07:38.763 --> 01:07:40.640
"What Makes a Person Human."

01:07:41.307 --> 01:07:42.892
By Kim Ro-sa.

01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:44.561
MY SONG, MY WIND

01:07:44.644 --> 01:07:47.522
What makes a person human

01:07:48.189 --> 01:07:52.860
Is love, pressed down just a little

01:07:53.820 --> 01:07:56.114
Pressed a little

01:07:56.739 --> 01:07:59.659
From above, below, and the sides

01:07:59.742 --> 01:08:03.621
Like freshly packed rice in a bowl

01:08:04.872 --> 01:08:09.460
Like an eraser worn down
From choosing kind words

01:08:09.544 --> 01:08:13.381
So that the warmth shared
Between two embraced bodies

01:08:13.965 --> 01:08:16.050
Won't escape

01:08:16.676 --> 01:08:18.720
Won't disappear

01:08:19.762 --> 01:08:21.681
And will become human

01:08:35.028 --> 01:08:36.321
You did great today.

01:08:37.071 --> 01:08:39.741
You did even better than in rehearsal.

01:08:39.824 --> 01:08:43.369
I saw you both come in.
Why are you always late?

01:08:43.453 --> 01:08:44.746
No, we weren't.

01:08:44.829 --> 01:08:46.831
We got here right on time.

01:08:47.999 --> 01:08:50.793
We were both late.
Why do I always get blamed?

01:08:52.795 --> 01:08:54.339
It's obvious.

01:08:54.422 --> 01:08:56.466
- You're always late to the restaurant.
- What?

01:08:56.549 --> 01:08:58.593
It was just five minutes,
and that was only yesterday.

01:08:58.676 --> 01:09:04.307
It's exam season.
Can't you cut your part-timer some slack?

01:09:04.390 --> 01:09:05.725
Ma'am.

01:09:05.808 --> 01:09:07.185
Are they your family?

01:09:07.268 --> 01:09:10.229
- Yes, she's my great-niece.
- I see.

01:09:10.730 --> 01:09:12.273
Let me take a photo of you three.

01:09:12.357 --> 01:09:14.192
- Stand over there.
- Okay.

01:09:14.984 --> 01:09:19.072
All right. One, two, three.

01:09:19.155 --> 01:09:20.698
Smile.

01:09:20.782 --> 01:09:23.284
One, two, three.

01:09:23.368 --> 01:09:25.953
This is the summer version

01:09:26.037 --> 01:09:28.539
of our popular product line,
"Tropical in Winter."

01:09:28.623 --> 01:09:30.875
We're using Rubysseom strawberries
as the main fruit

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:32.293
with a jewel theme,

01:09:32.377 --> 01:09:35.046
and we'll arrange
the other fruits to match.

01:09:35.129 --> 01:09:38.132
Strawberries tend to get bruised easily.

01:09:38.216 --> 01:09:40.677
Should we add ice packs
or cushioning for shipping?

01:09:40.760 --> 01:09:43.429
The Rubysseom variety isn't that soft,

01:09:43.513 --> 01:09:45.682
so a single-layer packaging
should be fine.

01:09:45.765 --> 01:09:47.100
Okay.

01:09:49.102 --> 01:09:52.522
Thank you for your time
in the meeting, Ms. Yu.

01:09:55.108 --> 01:09:58.194
Thanks for your hard work, Ms. Giselle.

01:09:58.986 --> 01:10:01.572
That name fits you so well.
It really suits you.

01:10:03.241 --> 01:10:05.660
You must have had a lot of offers.

01:10:05.743 --> 01:10:08.246
I owe you one. Thanks, friend.

01:10:09.205 --> 01:10:10.540
No. I should thank you.

01:10:10.623 --> 01:10:13.668
How's business?
Is it better than your old corporate job?

01:10:13.751 --> 01:10:17.338
Do you mean KFMC?
Are you still interested?

01:10:18.798 --> 01:10:21.050
That's how it is
for someone who fell short.

01:10:21.551 --> 01:10:23.636
No matter how much I like my current job,

01:10:24.262 --> 01:10:25.847
I get hung up on what I missed.

01:10:26.889 --> 01:10:29.183
This job suits you really well.

01:10:30.351 --> 01:10:31.519
I know.

01:10:32.353 --> 01:10:35.189
Want to grab a bite since you're here?
I'm off soon.

01:10:35.273 --> 01:10:36.899
Let's do it next time.

01:10:36.983 --> 01:10:39.652
I have to stop by somewhere today.

01:10:48.995 --> 01:10:50.204
Mi-rae!

01:10:53.583 --> 01:10:56.919
Sorry to keep you waiting.
I got slammed with work.

01:10:57.003 --> 01:10:59.255
You didn't have to rush.

01:10:59.839 --> 01:11:01.507
- Here.
- Oh my.

01:11:01.591 --> 01:11:03.468
Share it with your coworkers.

01:11:03.968 --> 01:11:06.637
They're sweet this year, so don't worry.

01:11:06.721 --> 01:11:10.349
You should've called ahead.
We can't even sit down for tea.

01:11:10.433 --> 01:11:12.351
Just seeing you is enough.

01:11:12.435 --> 01:11:14.020
You must be busy. Head back in.

01:11:14.771 --> 01:11:15.813
Thank you.

01:11:17.398 --> 01:11:19.108
I'm glad to see you're doing well.

01:11:20.735 --> 01:11:21.778
You too.

01:11:22.904 --> 01:11:24.197
Go on. Hurry.

01:11:24.280 --> 01:11:26.657
Okay. I'll visit the farm again soon.

01:11:27.867 --> 01:11:28.910
Bye.

01:11:31.078 --> 01:11:32.205
Thank you.

01:12:11.536 --> 01:12:12.787
Found you.

01:12:16.707 --> 01:12:18.000
Se-jin.

01:12:22.213 --> 01:12:23.506
How did you…

01:12:24.465 --> 01:12:27.510
See? I recognized you, Mi-rae.

01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:32.390
I'm back.

01:12:54.871 --> 01:12:58.457
Next time I go to Duson-ri,
I should bring back an extra photo album.

01:13:01.335 --> 01:13:02.587
What the heck?

01:13:02.670 --> 01:13:06.048
- Mi-rae says she's heading back now.
- I thought she was staying over tonight.

01:13:06.132 --> 01:13:09.802
Yes, but she met someone
and is heading home right now.

01:13:11.387 --> 01:13:13.347
Since I got stood up,

01:13:13.431 --> 01:13:15.308
I guess I'll just sleep here tonight.

01:13:16.559 --> 01:13:17.810
Tend to my needs.

01:13:17.894 --> 01:13:21.022
Have my pajamas been washed and ironed?

01:13:22.023 --> 01:13:24.317
They're in the drawer.

01:13:32.074 --> 01:13:33.409
My pajamas…

01:13:36.787 --> 01:13:37.914
What is this?

01:13:44.295 --> 01:13:45.212
What?

01:13:54.764 --> 01:13:56.057
Hey.

01:13:57.141 --> 01:14:00.394
Did you know that
a primary caregiver's view on marriage

01:14:00.478 --> 01:14:03.773
has a huge influence
on their child's view on marriage?

01:14:03.856 --> 01:14:05.024
Really?

01:14:05.107 --> 01:14:08.694
My mom says the best decision
she ever made was getting married.

01:14:08.778 --> 01:14:10.571
Well, my mom always said

01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:13.157
you should only get married

01:14:13.240 --> 01:14:16.160
when you can live on your own.

01:14:16.243 --> 01:14:19.497
She drilled that into my head so hard.
Total gaslighting.

01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:23.125
Honestly, marriage is
just a stamp on a document.

01:14:23.876 --> 01:14:25.378
What's the big deal, really?

01:14:25.461 --> 01:14:29.674
But still, it's the beginning
of a new chapter in life,

01:14:29.757 --> 01:14:33.594
so I want to start it
at the right time, with a clear mind.

01:14:33.678 --> 01:14:36.430
You know, it'll be…

01:14:37.348 --> 01:14:38.391
You…

01:14:39.350 --> 01:14:41.352
finally figured out what you want to be?

01:14:42.853 --> 01:14:43.854
Yes.

01:14:45.898 --> 01:14:47.400
A therapist.

01:14:48.651 --> 01:14:50.111
That's perfect for you.

01:14:50.194 --> 01:14:52.363
I knew you'd figure it out.
Congratulations.

01:14:52.947 --> 01:14:57.410
But apparently,
you need a master's degree for that.

01:14:58.119 --> 01:14:59.870
Then go to grad school.

01:14:59.954 --> 01:15:03.749
I feel bad, though.
For making you wait so long.

01:15:04.667 --> 01:15:08.629
Is this about getting your first paycheck
before getting married?

01:15:09.672 --> 01:15:11.632
A few years' delay doesn't matter.

01:15:11.716 --> 01:15:13.467
You've found what you want to do.

01:15:14.385 --> 01:15:18.639
Hey, aren't you a bit disappointed?

01:15:18.723 --> 01:15:21.726
I mean, who knows
how long you'll have to wait.

01:15:22.309 --> 01:15:23.561
You know,

01:15:24.228 --> 01:15:26.355
the one who loves more
is supposed to wait.

01:15:26.939 --> 01:15:28.274
And I'm good at waiting.

01:15:35.865 --> 01:15:38.075
Don't run off after saying all this.

01:15:39.326 --> 01:15:40.453
I won't.

01:15:55.593 --> 01:15:56.761
Gosh.

01:15:57.678 --> 01:15:59.096
- Hey.
- What?

01:15:59.180 --> 01:16:01.682
I swear, there's something in here.

01:16:01.766 --> 01:16:04.643
Every time I try to do something, I mean…

01:16:07.646 --> 01:16:08.647
Hello.

01:16:09.982 --> 01:16:12.026
I wasn't doing anything. Why?

01:16:15.154 --> 01:16:16.572
You want me to come home?

01:16:18.491 --> 01:16:19.617
With Ho-su?

01:16:20.493 --> 01:16:21.916
COUNTRY HOUSE IN SAEUL-DONG

01:16:21.987 --> 01:16:23.191
There.

01:16:23.287 --> 01:16:25.956
Remodeling? At the same time?

01:16:26.040 --> 01:16:27.666
No, one after the other.

01:16:28.167 --> 01:16:31.879
We'll stay at each other's places
while our houses are being remodeled.

01:16:32.379 --> 01:16:35.174
So you two need to take some stuff
and toss what you don't need.

01:16:35.257 --> 01:16:38.260
But my place is small.
Can't I leave things here?

01:16:38.344 --> 01:16:39.845
Take something.

01:16:40.554 --> 01:16:43.015
Isn't Ho-su moving into a bigger place?

01:16:43.099 --> 01:16:44.642
Keep some stuff there.

01:16:45.226 --> 01:16:46.602
Excuse me.

01:16:46.685 --> 01:16:48.521
Ho-su's place is not a storage unit.

01:16:49.146 --> 01:16:51.232
Why dump junk at a new home?

01:16:51.982 --> 01:16:54.652
Gosh, who said anything
about a storage unit?

01:16:55.152 --> 01:16:58.197
I never said to store junk, did I?

01:16:58.280 --> 01:17:01.534
Actually, I've been
meaning to tell you this.

01:17:02.076 --> 01:17:03.661
When I move…

01:17:07.706 --> 01:17:09.250
It'll be nice.

01:17:10.501 --> 01:17:12.044
- It must be.
- You're that happy?

01:17:12.128 --> 01:17:13.295
Yes.

01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:18.342
We agreed not to talk about that yet.

01:17:18.425 --> 01:17:19.791
We have to tell them eventually…

01:17:24.056 --> 01:17:25.516
We can't tell them.

01:17:25.599 --> 01:17:28.602
"Living together" isn't
in our primary caregivers' vocabulary.

01:17:28.686 --> 01:17:31.313
But you said you'd take
the spare room once your lease is up--

01:17:31.397 --> 01:17:34.316
I will, but why tell them now?

01:17:34.400 --> 01:17:37.069
Even if we don't,
they'll find out the second they visit.

01:17:37.153 --> 01:17:38.904
There's a way to keep it under the radar.

01:17:38.988 --> 01:17:40.739
Don't you know
my college friends live alone?

01:17:40.823 --> 01:17:43.075
Are you planning something shady again?

01:17:43.159 --> 01:17:44.702
Don't you want to live with me?

01:17:44.785 --> 01:17:47.496
I didn't mean it like that.

01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:50.291
I just think we should be honest.

01:17:50.374 --> 01:17:52.835
I'm not saying we should never tell them.

01:17:52.918 --> 01:17:56.255
I'll let them know when the time is right.

01:17:56.338 --> 01:17:58.215
Ho-su, I need you for a sec.

01:17:58.757 --> 01:17:59.842
All right.

01:18:01.302 --> 01:18:02.678
We'll tell them someday, okay?

01:18:05.306 --> 01:18:06.640
Grab another box for me.

01:18:07.725 --> 01:18:08.809
Sure.

01:18:47.932 --> 01:18:51.227
DECEMBER 3, 1995
THE DAY MI-RAE AND MI-JI WERE BORN

01:18:56.065 --> 01:18:57.566
85 DAYS IN THE WORLD

01:18:57.650 --> 01:18:59.777
92 DAYS IN THE WORLD

01:19:01.028 --> 01:19:02.404
MI-RAE, MI-JI
I LOVE YOU FOREVER

01:19:12.081 --> 01:19:14.708
I realized after going through
a few chapters

01:19:15.501 --> 01:19:17.503
that life isn't a book with an ending.

01:19:18.254 --> 01:19:21.257
It's a notebook I have to fill in myself.

01:19:24.051 --> 01:19:28.347
Even if I'm confronted by a blank page,
it's not the end, but a beginning.

01:19:31.684 --> 01:19:36.563
It's the unwritten first page of my story.

01:19:38.065 --> 01:19:43.279
There will surely be
unexpected twists and turns along the way…

01:19:43.362 --> 01:19:44.655
MI-JI, SEOUL!

01:19:45.572 --> 01:19:48.742
…but I'll keep searching
for a line of happiness

01:19:48.826 --> 01:19:50.828
and keep writing

01:19:51.870 --> 01:19:55.124
until I've filled every page.

01:20:14.852 --> 01:20:16.020
Mi-ji!

01:20:16.562 --> 01:20:17.646
Yes?

01:21:36.100 --> 01:21:38.685
MY SEOUL

01:21:42.024 --> 01:21:44.024
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
